Z||000003||FieroGT||06-23-2000||11:11 AM||||Actually, I can shed some light on the situation......<P>I am semi-active on another board that caters to the '89-'90 Pontiac Turbo Grand Prix's, since I have one. Dennis posted a turbo setup from a Turbo Grand Prix for sale, that only had about +/-20K on it. This post was made about a week ago. The turbo kit is designed to bolt onto an aluminum headed 3.1, which is what the TGP's used. <P>Unfortunately, it appears to me as if he's getting out of the business. <P>John||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||06-23-2000||06:51 PM||||Before he gits completely out, I sure would like to know how his turbo 3.4 Fiero project went. I've been doing a little reading on the subject of turbo charging and it soooo easy for a 3.4 turbo to pump out 300 hp. With the right pistons and detonation control maybe 350 hp.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Man, that kinda stuff just gets my motor running,<BR>Roy||||reg||9
